<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Anglo-Corsican Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1794 CE – 1796 CE · capital Bastia</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A two-year union of Corsica with the British crown, created by Pasquale Paoli to escape revolutionary France.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pasquale-paoli">Pasquale Paoli</a> returned to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a> in 1790 but broke with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-revolution">French Revolution</a>. In 1794, with British naval help, Corsican forces drove the French from the island; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/horatio-nelson">Nelson</a> lost the sight of an eye at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siege-of-calvi">siege of Calvi</a>. A Corsican assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corte">Corte</a> voted to offer the crown to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-iii">George III</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The kingdom had a liberal constitution with an elected parliament, under a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gilbert-elliot-1st-earl-of-minto">Sir Gilbert Elliot</a>, who governed from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bastia">Bastia</a>. Paoli expected to lead the government but was sidelined and left for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> in 1795. <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/united-kingdom">Britain</a> valued the island as a naval base in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon's</a> victories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1796 made the island hard to hold, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain's</a> alliance with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> threatened British naval control. The British evacuated <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/corsican-republic">Corsica</a> in October 1796, and it returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/french-first-republic">French First Republic</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/anglo-corsican-kingdom.jpg" alt="Anglo-Corsican Kingdom" width="320" height="192"><figcaption>Image: Samhanin (COA) / HapHaxion (Banner) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Anglo-Corsican_Kingdom.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1794 CE – 1796 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Bastia</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>George III, Sir Gilbert Elliot, Pasquale Paoli</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Corsican and Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/france">France</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Corsica (1794-1796)</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1795&amp;focus=anglo-corsican-kingdom" aria-label="Anglo-Corsican Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4909 660 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Anglo-Corsican Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5229 916L4997 651M5229 916L5054 728"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4997 651h0M5054 728h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5229 916h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5229 916h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Bastia. <a href="/atlas?year=1795&amp;focus=anglo-corsican-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

